# Summary
Introduced. The change to PG-scoped pending slots is not consistently reflected at the bucket-delete cleanup site: a function that previously removed only one bucket's pending command now removes the whole PG entry, and an existing caller still invokes it as if it were bucket-scoped.
Pending metadata commands are the recovery mechanism used when a metadata command is partially applied or must be retried. This commit changes LocalClusterRuntimeState.pending_metadata_commands from a (PgId, BucketName) map to a PgId-only map, and clear_pending_metadata_command_for_bucket now ignores the bucket argument and removes the entire PG slot. However, delete_bucket_from_acting_set still calls clear_pending_metadata_command_for_bucket after deleting one finalized bucket, without checking whether the PG slot belongs to that bucket. If another bucket on the same PG has a pending metadata command at that time, the bucket-delete finalizer can erase that unrelated pending command. If the erased command represented a partial apply or an in-flight command that later fails and needs retry, the recovery path is lost, leaving replicas or metadata state inconsistent. Since metadata commands include bucket ACL/public-access settings, object commits/deletes, and multipart cleanup, this can lead to permanent metadata corruption or data loss under concurrency plus a partial-apply/failure condition.

# Resolution
Fixed in commit `580979d` (`Preserve unrelated pending metadata on bucket finalize`).

The bucket finalization path no longer clears the PG-scoped in-memory pending metadata slot after deleting one finalized bucket. That clear was stale bucket-scoped cleanup from before the pending map became PG-scoped. The bucket's own `MarkBucketDeleting` command is already drained and removed by `begin_bucket_delete`; finalization is the explicit direct finalized-delete exception and must not remove unrelated PG pending work.

Added regression coverage in `finalized_bucket_delete_preserves_unrelated_same_pg_pending_command`, which creates two buckets on the same metadata PG, installs a pending command for one bucket, finalizes deletion of the other, and asserts the unrelated pending command remains.

