# Validation
## Rubric
- [x] Confirm the commit made pending metadata command slots PG-scoped rather than `(PgId, BucketName)` scoped.
- [x] Confirm `clear_pending_metadata_command_for_bucket` ignores the bucket and removes the entire PG slot.
- [x] Confirm bucket-delete finalization still invokes the bucket-named clear routine after deleting only one bucket and does not verify pending-command ownership.
- [x] Reproduce dynamically with two buckets on the same metadata PG where one bucket has an unrelated pending command while the other bucket is finalized for deletion.
- [x] Attempt direct crash/failing PoC, Valgrind/ASan-style validation, and debugger tracing before final code-understanding conclusion.
## Report
Validated the finding with a targeted Rust unit-test PoC. Code evidence: `crates/storage/src/cluster/local.rs:219` stores `pending_metadata_commands` as `HashMap<PgId, MetadataCommandEnvelope>`, so slots are PG-scoped. `local.rs:365-374` implements `clear_pending_metadata_command_for_bucket` by ignoring `bucket` and calling `.remove(&pg_id)`. `crates/storage/src/cluster/request_ops.rs:956-989` finalizes deletion of one bucket and then unconditionally calls `clear_pending_metadata_command_for_bucket(pg_id, bucket)`, with no check that the PG-scoped pending command belongs to the deleted bucket. I added a PoC test that creates two buckets mapped to metadata PG 1, marks one bucket deleting, manually installs a pending `PutBucketVersioning` command for the other bucket in the same PG slot, finalizes deletion of the first bucket, and asserts the survivor bucket's pending command remains. On commit 513501e0ff209f922da7f9bee2dffb1c97811c65, the test panics because the pending command is gone: `left: None`, `right: Some(MetadataCommandEnvelope ... bucket: "pending-survivor-1" ...)`. This directly reproduces the suspected cross-bucket pending-command loss. I also attempted Valgrind; it is not installed in the container (`bash: command not found: valgrind`). I ran LLDB non-interactively and set a breakpoint at `request_ops.rs:986`; the backtrace showed `try_finalize_bucket_delete` -> `delete_bucket_from_acting_set` immediately before the unconditional call to `.clear_pending_metadata_command_for_bucket(pg_id, bucket)`, followed by the PoC assertion failure.

